= Synthetic orchard study

Alpha trees grow beside the river, as described by @moss2020.
Beta birds sing above the meadow and gather
around the fountain at dusk.

Gamma clouds drift across the valley.#footnote[Delta stones rest beneath the willow.]

== Method

Epsilon seeds travel towards the orchard in three steps:

- Zeta leaves gather around the fountain.
- Eta roots stretch below the garden wall.
- Theta petals open in the morning light.

The relation between the three paths follows a simple rule, as @reed2018 notes:

$ a^2 + b^2 = c^2 $

== Results

All words in this fixture describe an invented orchard, and #underline(offset: 2pt, [iota moss covers the north wall]) in every season.

